description:
pkix-path: check_critical_extensions(cert) -> bool, then caller does:
  if !check_critical_extensions(cert) { return Err(Error::UnhandledCriticalExtension { index: i }); }
Idiomatic Rust uses Result to propagate errors, not bool + manual conversion at the call site. The function should take index and return Result<()>, letting the caller just use ?. Same pattern issue in check_validity which returns bool.
